  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.4.0 - The previewers work.\n\nOpening any control's style file in the IDE previewer now renders the control as it actually looks, in both themes, side by side. It never has before: the previews have been broken since v1.0.0 and failed silently, showing bare unstyled controls with no error.\n\nThis matters if you have cloned or forked the repository to read, learn from or modify the styles. If you only consume the package, nothing you see at runtime changes - Design.PreviewWith content is used by the designer and never instantiated by your app.\n\nThree separate faults had to be fixed, each enough on its own to keep the previewer dark: a style file previewed alone could not resolve the theme brushes its setters reference; the library had no entry point, so the previewer could not start; and the style files carried a build action that stopped Visual Studio offering a preview at all.\n\nAdded Invariant_7 to the test suite, which parses each preview in isolation and fails if it cannot resolve every resource key it references, under both theme variants.\n\nNo migration needed - nothing renamed, removed or restyled. Same single StyleInclude entry point, same 15 controls, still net10.0, still Avalonia 12.1.3.",
